{
  "capitulo": 1,
  "titulo_es": "¿Cómo se escribe?",
  "titulo": { "en": "How do you spell it?" },
  "intro": { "en": "In class you will need four questions: how to say something, how to spell it, what it means, and a way to ask for it again, more slowly." },
  "palabras": {
    "el abecedario": { "en": "the alphabet", "pron": "el a-be-the-DA-ryo", "genero": "m", "consejo": "C and z sound like the th in think, in most of Spain." },
    "la eñe": { "en": "the letter ñ", "pron": "la E-nye", "genero": "f", "nota": "Ñ is its own letter, between n and o. It sounds like ny in canyon." },
    "la hache": { "en": "the letter h", "pron": "la A-che", "genero": "f", "consejo": "The letter h is silent. Hola and hora start with a vowel sound." },
    "la jota": { "en": "the letter j", "pron": "la HO-ta", "genero": "f", "consejo": "J is a strong h, as in José. It is not the English j of José." },
    "se dice": { "en": "you say, it is called", "pron": "se DI-the", "cat": "expression" },
    "se escribe": { "en": "it is spelled", "pron": "se es-KRI-be", "cat": "expression" },
    "deletrear": { "en": "to spell out", "pron": "de-le-tre-AR", "cat": "verb" },
    "qué significa": { "en": "what does it mean", "pron": "ke sig-ni-FI-ka", "cat": "expression" },
    "no entiendo": { "en": "I don't understand", "pron": "no en-TYEN-do", "cat": "expression" },
    "más despacio": { "en": "more slowly", "pron": "mas des-PA-thyo", "cat": "expression" },
    "repite": { "en": "repeat (tú)", "pron": "re-PI-te", "cat": "verb" },
    "por favor": { "en": "please", "pron": "por fa-BOR", "cat": "expression" },
    "la mesa": { "en": "the table", "pron": "la ME-sa", "genero": "f" },
    "España": { "en": "Spain", "pron": "es-PA-nya", "nota": "España is spelled with ñ." }
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Questions you will use every day",
      "texto": "Four sentences carry a class.\n\n- **¿Cómo se dice** table **en español**?\n- **¿Cómo se escribe**?\n- **¿Qué significa** mesa?\n- **No entiendo. Más despacio, por favor.**\n\nThe alphabet is the English one plus **ñ**. In most of Spain, **c** before e or i, and **z**, sound like th in think: gracias, cero. **H** is silent. **J** is a hard h. **Ll** sounds like the English y in yes."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "titulo": "Letters that surprise English speakers",
      "columnas": ["Letter", "Sound in Spain", "Example"],
      "filas": [
        ["h", "silent", "hola"],
        ["j", "strong h", "jota"],
        ["ñ", "ny, as in canyon", "España"],
        ["ll", "y, as in yes", "llama"],
        ["z, ce, ci", "th, as in think", "cero"]
      ],
      "nota": { "en": "You do not need every letter name today. You need to ask, and to hear ñ, j and the silent h." }
    },
